<title>UK: Prism confirms shortlisted for 2 rail bids.</title>
<headline>Prism confirms shortlisted for 2 rail bids.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Prism Rail Plc said on Monday it had been shortlisted to operate the franchises for North West Regional Railways Ltd and Scotrail Railways Ltd.</p>
<p>Only 12 of Britain's 25 train operating companies remain in state hands and the government hopes to sell as many as possible ahead of a general election due by May.</p>
<p>Prism's statement did not mention the names of other bidders.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44-171-542 7717</p>
</text>
